{"id":"mahabharata-1-134","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":134,"title":"चतुस्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 134 · Yudhishthira detects the house of lac","summary":{"en":"Welcomed by the people of Varanavata, the Pandavas move into the new house. Smelling fat and lac, Yudhishthira tells Bhima it is built to burn them; rather than flee, they will live there watchfully and find a way of escape.","kn":"ವಾರಣಾವತದ ಜನರ ಸ್ವಾಗತದ ನಂತರ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಹೊಸ ಮನೆಗೆ ಬರುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕೊಬ್ಬು ಅರಗಿನ ವಾಸನೆಯಿಂದ ಇದು ತಮ್ಮನ್ನು ಸುಡಲೆಂದು ಕಟ್ಟಿದ ಮನೆ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಓಡಿಹೋಗದೆ ಎಚ್ಚರದಿಂದ ಅಲ್ಲೇ ಇದ್ದು ತಪ್ಪಿಸಿಕೊಳ್ಳುವ ದಾರಿ ಹುಡುಕೋಣ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वारणावत के लोगों के स्वागत के बाद पाण्डव नए भवन में रहने लगते हैं। चर्बी और लाख की गन्ध से युधिष्ठिर भीम से कहते हैं कि यह उन्हें जलाने के लिए बना है; भागने के बजाय वे सावधान होकर वहीं रहेंगे और बचने का उपाय खोजेंगे।","te":"వారణావత ప్రజల స్వాగతం తర్వాత పాండవులు కొత్త ఇంట్లోకి వస్తారు. కొవ్వు, లక్క వాసనతో ఇది తమను కాల్చడానికి కట్టిన ఇల్లని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు భీమునికి చెబుతాడు; పారిపోకుండా జాగ్రత్తగా అక్కడే ఉండి తప్పించుకునే మార్గం వెతుకుదామంటాడు.","ta":"வாரணாவத மக்களின் வரவேற்புக்குப் பின் பாண்டவர்கள் புதிய மாளிகையில் குடியேறுகிறார்கள். கொழுப்பு, அரக்கின் மணத்தால் இது தம்மை எரிக்கக் கட்டப்பட்டது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் பீமனிடம் சொல்கிறார்; ஓடாமல் விழிப்புடன் அங்கேயே தங்கித் தப்பும் வழியைக் காண்போம் என்கிறார்.","ml":"വാരണാവതത്തിലെ ജനങ്ങൾ സ്വീകരിക്കുമ്പോൾ പാണ്ഡവർ പുതിയ ഗൃഹത്തിൽ പാർക്കുന്നു. കൊഴുപ്പിന്റെയും അരക്കിന്റെയും ഗന്ധം മണത്ത യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ, തങ്ങളെ ചുട്ടുകൊല്ലാനാണ് ഇത് പണിതതെന്ന് ഭീമനോട് പറയുന്നു; ഓടിരക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നതിനുപകരം അവർ ജാഗ്രതയോടെ അവിടെ പാർത്ത് രക്ഷപ്പെടാൻ വഴി കണ്ടെത്താൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.134; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जतुगृहपर्व","titleEn":"Jatugriha Parva (The house of lac)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः सर्वाः प्रकृतयो नगराद्वारणावतात् ।\nसर्वमङ्गलसंयुक्ता यथाशास्त्रमतन्द्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the townsfolk of Varanavata, hearing of the Pandavas' arrival, set out from the city, dressed for festivity and eager, with every auspicious offering as the rules prescribe."}},{"n":2,"text":"श्रुत्वागतान्पाण्डुपुत्रान्नानायानैः सहस्रशः ।\nअभिजग्मुर्नरश्रेष्ठाञ्श्रुत्वैव परया मुदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard that the sons of Pandu had come, those people came out in thousands in all kinds of conveyances, greatly delighted to meet the best of men."}},{"n":3,"text":"ते समासाद्य कौन्तेयान्वारणावतका जनाः ।\nकृत्वा जयाशिषः सर्वे परिवार्योपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people of Varanavata reached the sons of Kunti, spoke blessings of victory over them, and stood around them in attendance."}},{"n":4,"text":"तैर्वृतः पुरुषव्याघ्रो धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nविबभौ देवसंकाशो वज्रपाणिरिवामरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by them, Yudhishthira, the tiger among men and king of dharma, shone like Indra, wielder of the thunderbolt, amid the gods."}},{"n":5,"text":"सत्कृतास्ते तु पौरैश्च पौरान्सत्कृत्य चानघाः ।\nअलंकृतं जनाकीर्णं विविशुर्वारणावतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blameless brothers were honored by the citizens and honored them in turn, and then entered Varanavata, which was decked out and thronged with people."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते प्रविश्य पुरं वीरास्तूर्णं जग्मुरथो गृहान् ।\nब्राह्मणानां महीपाल रतानां स्वेषु कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering the city, the heroes went at once to the homes of Brahmins who were devoted to their own duties, O king."}},{"n":7,"text":"नगराधिकृतानां च गृहाणि रथिनां तथा ।\nउपतस्थुर्नरश्रेष्ठा वैश्यशूद्रगृहानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those best of men also visited the houses of the city's officials and of charioteers, and even the homes of Vaishyas and Shudras."}},{"n":8,"text":"अर्चिताश्च नरैः पौरैः पाण्डवा भरतर्षभाः ।\nजग्मुरावसथं पश्चात्पुरोचनपुरस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored by the townspeople, the Pandavas, bulls of the Bharata line, afterwards went to their lodging with Purochana leading the way."}},{"n":9,"text":"तेभ्यो भक्ष्यान्नपानानि शयनानि शुभानि च ।\nआसनानि च मुख्यानि प्रददौ स पुरोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Purochana gave them food and drink, fine beds, and choice seats."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्र ते सत्कृतास्तेन सुमहार्हपरिच्छदाः ।\nउपास्यमानाः पुरुषैरूषुः पुरनिवासिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored by him there, and provided with very costly furnishings, they lived attended by the men of the city."}},{"n":11,"text":"दशरात्रोषितानां तु तत्र तेषां पुरोचनः ।\nनिवेदयामास गृहं शिवाख्यमशिवं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had stayed ten nights, Purochana showed them a house named 'Shiva' (auspicious), which in fact was anything but auspicious."}},{"n":12,"text":"तत्र ते पुरुषव्याघ्रा विविशुः सपरिच्छदाः ।\nपुरोचनस्य वचनात्कैलासमिव गुह्यकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tigers among men entered it with their belongings, on Purochana's word, like Guhyakas entering Kailasa."}},{"n":13,"text":"तत्त्वगारमभिप्रेक्ष्य सर्वधर्मविशारदः ।\nउवाचाग्नेयमित्येवं भीमसेनं युधिष्ठिरः ।\nजिघ्रन्सोम्य वसागन्धं सर्पिर्जतुविमिश्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surveying the house, Yudhishthira, who knew all the duties, told Bhima that it was built to burn: 'Smell it, gentle Bhima, the odor of fat and ghee mixed with lac.'"}},{"n":14,"text":"कृतं हि व्यक्तमाग्नेयमिदं वेश्म परंतप ।\nशणसर्जरसं व्यक्तमानीतं गृहकर्मणि ।\nमुञ्जबल्वजवंशादि द्रव्यं सर्वं घृतोक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Clearly, scorcher of foes, this house has been made flammable. Flax, resin and the other materials brought for its building, with reed, grass and bamboo, are all soaked in ghee."}},{"n":15,"text":"शिल्पिभिः सुकृतं ह्याप्तैर्विनीतैर्वेश्मकर्मणि ।\nविश्वस्तं मामयं पापो दग्धुकामः पुरोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Skilled and trusted craftsmen, well trained in house-building, have made it, and the wicked Purochana wants to burn me while I trust him."}},{"n":16,"text":"इमां तु तां महाबुद्धिर्विदुरो दृष्टवांस्तदा ।\nआपदं तेन मां पार्थ स संबोधितवान्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"'The wise Vidura foresaw this danger long ago, son of Pritha, and so he warned me."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते वयं बोधितास्तेन बुद्धवन्तोऽशिवं गृहम् ।\nआचार्यैः सुकृतं गूढैर्दुर्योधनवशानुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Warned by him, we have recognized this house as deadly, secretly built by artisans who serve Duryodhana's will.'"}},{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"यदिदं गृहमाग्नेयं विहितं मन्यते भवान् ।\nतत्रैव साधु गच्छामो यत्र पूर्वोषिता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'If you think this house is a fire-trap, then let us go back to where we stayed before.'"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"इह यत्तैर्निराकारैर्वस्तव्यमिति रोचये ।\nनष्टैरिव विचिन्वद्भिर्गतिमिष्टां ध्रुवामितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I think we should stay here, looking unsuspecting, while we search for a sure way of escape, as if we had lost our way."}},{"n":20,"text":"यदि विन्देत चाकारमस्माकं हि पुरोचनः ।\nशीघ्रकारी ततो भूत्वा प्रसह्यापि दहेत नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'If Purochana discovers any sign of our intent, he will act swiftly and burn us by force."}},{"n":21,"text":"नायं बिभेत्युपक्रोशादधर्माद्वा पुरोचनः ।\nतथा हि वर्तते मन्दः सुयोधनमते स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Purochana fears neither blame nor sin, for the fool follows Suyodhana's wishes."}},{"n":22,"text":"अपि चेह प्रदग्धेषु भीष्मोऽस्मासु पितामहः ।\nकोपं कुर्यात्किमर्थं वा कौरवान्कोपयेत सः ।\nधर्म इत्येव कुप्येत तथान्ये कुरुपुंगवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'And if we were burned here, why would Grandfather Bhishma be angry, or why would he anger the Kauravas? Other Kuru chiefs would grumble only that it was wrong."}},{"n":23,"text":"वयं तु यदि दाहस्य बिभ्यतः प्रद्रवेम हि ।\nस्पशैर्नो घातयेत्सार्वान्राज्यलुब्धः सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'But if we ran away in fear of being burned, Suyodhana, greedy for the kingdom, would have us killed by spies."}},{"n":24,"text":"अपदस्थान्पदे तिष्ठन्नपक्षान्पक्षसंस्थितः ।\nहीनकोशान्महाकोशः प्रयोगैर्घातयेद्ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'He holds the position while we have none, he has allies while we have none, he has a full treasury while ours is empty; he will surely kill us by schemes."}},{"n":25,"text":"तदस्माभिरिमं पापं तं च पापं सुयोधनम् ।\nवञ्चयद्भिर्निवस्तव्यं छन्नवासं क्वचित्क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'So we must live in disguise, now here, now there, deceiving this sinner and that sinner Suyodhana."}},{"n":26,"text":"ते वयं मृगयाशीलाश्चराम वसुधामिमाम् ।\nतथा नो विदिता मार्गा भविष्यन्ति पलायताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'We shall roam this earth as hunters, so that we come to know the paths by which we might flee."}},{"n":27,"text":"भौमं च बिलमद्यैव करवाम सुसंवृतम् ।\nगूढोच्छ्वसान्न नस्तत्र हुताशः संप्रधक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'And let us this very day dig a well-hidden underground tunnel; then, breathing unseen inside it, the fire will not consume us."}},{"n":28,"text":"वसतोऽत्र यथा चास्मान्न बुध्येत पुरोचनः ।\nपौरो वापि जनः कश्चित्तथा कार्यमतन्द्रितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'We must live here, alert, in such a way that neither Purochana nor any townsman notices.'"}}]}]}